  "fidelityReview": {
    "target": "maximum",
    "status": "passed",
    "scope": "Detailed exterior world-viewer representation with stated reconstruction limits.",
    "notes": "Detailed 311.8 m exterior accepted for world-viewer use: stepped red-granite shaft with narrow dark glazing ribbons, paired windowed corner piers, projecting fins and recessed spandrels; four deep elliptical archivolt portals with brass-framed doors, raised walks and planters; separately mapped mirrored-glass west wing; open stepped crown with closely spaced circular Atlanta Rouge aluminum tubes, steel bracing, catwalks, ladder and floodlight housings; and the original documented 90 ft gold-leaf obelisk. Intermediate datums, exact tube/facade schedules and minor crest carving are reconstructed from original architect and Architectural Record photographs plus firsthand entrance references. Dynamic night lighting, tenant interiors and future west-wing redevelopment are excluded."
  }
